# Ansible's Hetzner credentials. Copy this file to ansible/.envrc (gitignored)
# and fill in the real values:
#   cp .envrc.example .envrc
#   direnv allow
#
# Without direnv, `source .envrc` from this directory once per shell -- these
# are plain exports. That is a full alternative here and not a fallback with a
# catch: neither name is the HCLOUD_TOKEN that the repository-root and
# terraform/stacks/main-staging/ .envrc files both export with DIFFERENT
# values, where an export outliving its directory is a real hazard. See
# docs/bootstrap-a-new-host.md 4.1 for that one, and 6.0 for this one.
#
# BOTH ARE READ ONLY TOKENS. Never put a Read & Write token here: each stack's
# lives exclusively in that stack's own GitHub Environment secret, and a stack
# whose Environment requires no reviewer is no exception. See AGENTS.md.
#
# ONE VARIABLE PER STACK, because a Hetzner token is scoped to one project and
# each stack has a project of its own. Each name is read by exactly one
# inventory source -- inventory/main-production.hcloud.yml and
# inventory/main-staging.hcloud.yml -- so which project a run reaches is decided
# by the source it names with `-i`, not by what a shell happens to export.
# Bringing a third stack into inventory adds a source and a line here.
#
# THE VARIABLE NAMES ARE THE STACK, NOT THE ENVIRONMENT AXIS. They match the
# repository secrets each stack's pipeline.yml declares, which is an obligation
# rather than a coincidence: the converge job holds the credential under the
# declared name and exports it under the name the inventory source reads, and
# `.github/tests` compares the pair. `MAIN_` is there because repository
# secrets are one flat namespace and the environment alone stops being unique
# at a second tenant -- see the production stack's pipeline.yml.
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT THE REPOSITORY-ROOT .envrc, AND THE DIFFERENCE MATTERS.
# That one exports HCLOUD_TOKEN, which is what the *Terraform* provider reads,
# and docs/bootstrap-a-new-host.md §4.1 scopes it per stack directory --
# main-production's at the root, main-staging's inside
# terraform/stacks/main-staging/.
# direnv loads the nearest .envrc and does not merge the parent's, so in this
# directory HCLOUD_TOKEN is not set at all. That is deliberate: nothing Ansible
# reads shares a name with a variable whose value depends on where you stand.
#
# A wrong or missing value fails the run rather than producing a group with no
# host in it -- ansible.cfg's `any_unparsed_is_failed`. Without that, a typo
# here would look exactly like a destroyed server.
export HCLOUD_TOKEN_MAIN_PRODUCTION="your-read-only-hetzner-token-for-main-productions-project"
export HCLOUD_TOKEN_MAIN_STAGING="your-read-only-hetzner-token-for-main-stagings-project"
